                    <occupation>OCCUPATION</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>See Ed Pope's notes: Possibly Richard Langslow MD died Hot Wells Bristol
                            24.12.1813 aged 60, will PCC 1813 (wife Sarah will PCC 1816) former
                            physician to Lying In Charity, London, practised in Suffolk in
                            partnership with Courtenay and with Miles Rudland, surgeons, left Suffolk
                            1805. See Alexander. There are reasons to think Alexander was a medical
                            professional but it's not certain, the four entries in six days 1808 are
                            interesting, why Accounts? And Ash was certainly a doctor though his
                            call might have been a coincidence </p>
